  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Merged Districts (KPMD) Support Programme (previously called the Federally Administered Tribal Areas (FATA) Development Programme)-Delivery through United Nations Agencies - Phase I</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Merged Districts (KPMD) Support Programme (previously called the Federally Administered Tribal Areas (FATA) Development Programme)-Delivery through United Nations Agencies - Phase I is a component of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Merged Districts (KPMD) Support Programme (previously called the Federally Administered Tribal Areas (FATA) Development Programme) reported by FCDO with a funding type of 109 - Multilateral organisation and a budget of &#xa3;33,951,700. It works in the following sector(s): Civilian peace-building, conflict prevention and resolution, Primary education, Basic health care, Legal and judicial development, Public finance management (PFM), Public sector policy and administrative management.</narrative>
  </description>
